  "factor_name": "Close-Location-Value Shock Reversal",
  "version": "1.0",
  "calculation": {
    "expression": "shift_1((-relative_return_10d/(volatility_20d*sqrt(10))) * (1 + 0.6*clip(rolling_mean_5(-CLV),0,1)))",
    "description": "Cross-sectional reversal of the asset's 10-day return relative to the contemporaneous cross-sectional median, normalized by 20-day volatility and amplified when recent daily closes are near their lows. CLV=(2*close-high-low)/(high-low); the complete signal is lagged one trading day."
